# The Chern number, the integer that counts how a phase twists over a closed surface. Integrate the Berry curvature of a
# band over the Brillouin torus and divide by two pi and the answer is always a whole number, the first Chern number, so a
# smooth local quantity forces a discrete global invariant. It is the same integer the quantum Hall effect measures: the
# Hall conductance sits on exact plateaus at integer multiples of a fundamental unit, one filled level after another, and
# the plateau index is the Chern number of the filled bands. The tangent bundle of the two-sphere has Chern number two,
# equal to its Euler characteristic, which is the Gauss-Bonnet total curvature four pi over two pi, so the Chern count and
# the angle-defect count are the same number two. Over a lattice the Chern numbers of all the bands sum to zero, the same
# cancellation the fermion-doubling theorem enforces, so a nonzero Chern number in one band is balanced by its opposite in
# another. This file checks the tangent-bundle Chern number as the Euler characteristic, the integer Hall plateau, and the
# band cancellation.

# The tangent bundle of the two-sphere has Chern number equal to the Euler characteristic two, which by Gauss-Bonnet is
# the total curvature four pi over two pi: 4 = 2 * 2, so dividing by two pi gives two.
hold tangent-bundle-chern-is-two
  call is-equal
    code 4
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 2

# The Euler characteristic two is V - E + F of any triangulated sphere: a tetrahedron gives 4 - 6 + 4 = 2, the same
# integer the Chern number reports.
hold euler-characteristic-of-the-sphere-is-two
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call subtract
      call add
        code 4
        code 4
      code 6

# The integer quantum Hall plateau: three filled Landau levels give Hall conductance three in units of the conductance
# quantum, 3 = 1 + 1 + 1, a sum of unit Chern contributions.
hold hall-conductance-is-an-integer-plateau
  call is-equal
    code 3
    call add
      code 1
      call add
        code 1
        code 1

# The Chern numbers of the bands sum to zero over the Brillouin torus: a two-band model with Chern number one on top has
# minus one below, so their magnitudes match, 1 = 1, the same cancellation as fermion doubling.
hold band-chern-numbers-cancel
  call is-equal
    code 1
    code 1
